[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=2.2]
\draw[step=0.2,gray!30,very thin] (-1,-1) grid (1,1);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-1.25,0)--(1.25,0) node[right,font=\scriptsize]{$x$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,-1.25)--(0,1.25) node[above,font=\scriptsize]{$y$};
\draw (0,0) circle (1);
\node[below right,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$O$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (1,0) {$1$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (-1,0) {$-1$};
\node[right,font=\scriptsize] at (0,1) {$1$};
\node[right,font=\scriptsize] at (0,-1) {$-1$};
\coordinate (P) at (-0.8,0.6);
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0)--(P);
\fill[red] (P) circle (1.4pt);
\node[above left,font=\scriptsize] at (P) {$P$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The point $P(\cos\theta,\sin\theta)$ is shown on the unit circle. Use the grid to state $\cos\theta$ and $\sin\theta$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=2]
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-1.3,0)--(1.3,0) node[right,font=\scriptsize]{$x$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,-1.3)--(0,1.3) node[above,font=\scriptsize]{$y$};
\draw (0,0) circle (1);
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (240:1);
\draw[thick,blue] (O)--(P);
\draw (0.32,0) arc (0:240:0.32);
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (120:0.6) {$240^{\circ}$};
\fill[red] (P) circle (1.2pt);
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (P) {$P$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The radius to $P$ makes an angle of $240^{\circ}$ with the positive $x$-axis. Which coordinate of $P$ gives $\sin\theta$, and what is its sign?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=2]
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-1.3,0)--(1.3,0) node[right,font=\scriptsize]{$x$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,-1.3)--(0,1.3) node[above,font=\scriptsize]{$y$};
\draw (0,0) circle (1);
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (160:1);
\draw[thick,blue] (O)--(P);
\draw (0.32,0) arc (0:160:0.32);
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (80:0.6) {$160^{\circ}$};
\fill[red] (P) circle (1.2pt);
\node[above left,font=\scriptsize] at (P) {$P$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The radius to $P$ makes an angle of $160^{\circ}$ with the positive $x$-axis. Which coordinate of $P$ gives $\cos\theta$, and what is its sign?
